From: Marionette AirDrop driver research
Subject: [EXPERIMENTAL] give the monitor vdev a TX lifecycle and admit mission mode

Static audit of the 0003 injection prototype found two independent reasons the
entry can never deliver a frame in the coexistence configuration:

1. hdd_mon_awdl_start_xmit() required cds_get_conparam() ==
   QDF_GLOBAL_MONITOR_MODE (4).  The device runs QDF_GLOBAL_MISSION_MODE (0),
   which is the only mode in which the station stays associated, so the gate
   rejected every frame before any other check ran.

2. dp_vdev_attach_wifi3() returns from the monitor branch immediately after
   dp_monitor_vdev_attach(), so dp_tx_vdev_attach() never ran and
   vdev->htt_tcl_metadata stayed zeroed.  dp_tx_vdev_attach() is what writes
   DP_TCL_METADATA_TYPE_VDEV_BASED and this vdev's id/pdev id into the TCL
   metadata; without it an injected frame is described as vdev 0, i.e. the
   station, and vdev->tx_encap_type is never set at all (dp_tx.c:1289 copies it
   into the SW descriptor, and dp_tx.c:1699/1785/3579 branch on it).

Both are host-side only.  No firmware command value, ring layout, descriptor
format, channel, rate or retry setting is changed.  The exception path itself
was already viable: the monitor vdev is inserted into the DP vdev id map at
dp_main.c:7107 before the branch, dp_check_exc_metadata() accepts
tid=0/encap=raw/sec=none, and the non-STA address-search default does not
dereference a peer.

What this does NOT establish: whether the firmware accepts a TCL descriptor
built on an unassociated monitor vdev at all.  That is the real open question
and the reason the parameter stays default-off.

Acceptance must not be the send() return value.  Host enqueue returning NULL
only means a descriptor was written to the TCL ring.  OTA proof requires an
externally observable effect.

diff --git a/qca-wifi-host-cmn/dp/wifi3.0/dp_main.c b/qca-wifi-host-cmn/dp/wifi3.0/dp_main.c
index 76bb707..3c869e4 100644
--- a/qca-wifi-host-cmn/dp/wifi3.0/dp_main.c
+++ b/qca-wifi-host-cmn/dp/wifi3.0/dp_main.c
@@ -7113,6 +7113,20 @@ static QDF_STATUS dp_vdev_attach_wifi3(struct cdp_soc_t *cdp_soc,
 
 	if (wlan_op_mode_monitor == vdev->opmode) {
 		if (dp_monitor_vdev_attach(vdev) == QDF_STATUS_SUCCESS) {
+			/*
+			 * Marionette: dp_vdev_attach_wifi3() returns here for
+			 * monitor vdevs, so dp_tx_vdev_attach() never runs and
+			 * vdev->htt_tcl_metadata stays zeroed.  An injected
+			 * frame would then be described with vdev_id 0 and the
+			 * wrong metadata type, i.e. attributed to the station.
+			 * Build the TCL metadata for this vdev and declare RAW
+			 * encapsulation so the descriptor carries an already
+			 * formed 802.11 frame instead of an Ethernet payload.
+			 * Address-search flags fall to the non-STA default,
+			 * which is what an unassociated injector needs.
+			 */
+			vdev->tx_encap_type = htt_cmn_pkt_type_raw;
+			dp_tx_vdev_attach(vdev);
 			dp_monitor_pdev_set_mon_vdev(vdev);
 			return dp_monitor_vdev_set_monitor_mode_buf_rings(pdev);
 		}
diff --git a/qcacld-3.0/core/hdd/src/wlan_hdd_tx_rx.c b/qcacld-3.0/core/hdd/src/wlan_hdd_tx_rx.c
index 17a2a10..f895808 100644
--- a/qcacld-3.0/core/hdd/src/wlan_hdd_tx_rx.c
+++ b/qcacld-3.0/core/hdd/src/wlan_hdd_tx_rx.c
@@ -681,6 +681,7 @@ netdev_tx_t hdd_mon_awdl_start_xmit(struct sk_buff *skb, struct net_device *dev)
 	struct hdd_adapter *adapter;
 	ol_txrx_soc_handle soc;
 	struct cdp_tx_exception_metadata metadata = {0};
+	enum QDF_GLOBAL_MODE con_mode;
 	u8 *frame;
 	unsigned int bytes;
 
@@ -688,8 +689,14 @@ netdev_tx_t hdd_mon_awdl_start_xmit(struct sk_buff *skb, struct net_device *dev)
 	adapter = WLAN_HDD_GET_PRIV_PTR(dev);
 	/* Only filin's known radiotap layout and plain IPv6 AWDL data frames.
 	 * Management frames require a separate, verified WMI submission path. */
+	/* Marionette: mission mode is the only global mode in which the
+	 * station can stay associated, so the AWDL injector has to work
+	 * there. The monitor-adapter check and the frame-shape checks below
+	 * remain the real gates; global monitor mode stays accepted. */
+	con_mode = cds_get_conparam();
 	if (!READ_ONCE(marionette_awdl_raw_tx) ||
-	    cds_get_conparam() != QDF_GLOBAL_MONITOR_MODE ||
+	    (con_mode != QDF_GLOBAL_MONITOR_MODE &&
+	     con_mode != QDF_GLOBAL_MISSION_MODE) ||
 	    adapter->device_mode != QDF_MONITOR_MODE ||
 	    adapter->vdev_id == 0xff || skb->len < 13 + 24 + 16 + 40 ||
 	    skb->len > 13 + 2304 || skb_linearize(skb) ||
